    "created_at": "2026-06-27T18:21:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-27T18:21:30Z",
    "body": "I recall seeing a real world web server do `gzip, gzip` where the content was encoded accordingly. IMHO it's a fine use case.\nPlus otherwise it might further add to the complexity, e.g. would there be sufficient difference between `br, br, gzip` and `br, gzip, br` that one may be accepted while the other rejected (or both to be rejected)?",
